P1 — `.claude/plans/PLAN-166/repass-ga/run-ga-repass.sh:18` — `BASE_TAG=v1.2.0` is used without verifying its signature, remote object, peeled commit, or ancestry. A stale or accidentally moved local tag produces a valid, self-consistent but wrong `v1.2.0..rc.3` review payload that can receive GO. Minimal fix: bind the local base tag to one `ls-remote` snapshot, verify its signature and exact object/peel, require it to be an ancestor of RC3, and record both object IDs in provenance.

These two reachable P1s break pre-commit resumability and review-input provenance, so they must be fixed and re-reviewed before the cut.

